{"author":{"id":"f4e4dbe251fbd7519eab696986bae317e93a786739d6cebe9c4c1e89dd44e465"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793607318,"nonce":"VGPKEwR4FmZc6FdIrhn8hxAYq7Y=","message":"Changed after the 2026-11-02 document review (design §11 updated to match).\n\nExit criterion fixes. As written it could not pass: it asked for division and null-record tests in a milestone that rejects `/` and `%` and assumes non-null records.\n\n- Zero-divisor and `MinValue / -1` generators move to M6, which now models `/` and `%`. In M4, methods using `/`, `%` or checked arithmetic must be rejected with the M4 diagnostic, and the corpus contains such methods.\n- Null-record inputs check that .NET throws and that the non-null assumption is recorded. They are not compared against the model.\n- CLR-agreement tests (§10.6) pass for every operation M4 models. This was in scope but missing from the exit criterion.\n- `scripts/cross-check.sh` only runs its fixed corpus, so \"passes cross-check\" held without checking translated code. M4 adds a step that exports the translated corpus together with its Init + semantics closure as one 3.1.0 file and requires `lean-replay` to accept it. M5a and M6 add their certificates to that step.\n- The fixed corpus lives at `tests/corpus/m4/`. Minimum contents: `int`/`long`/`bool` arithmetic and comparisons, records, enums, `if`/`switch`, the `Validate`-shaped method, and one expected-rejection method per rejected construct (`/`, `%`, `checked`, and the open-enum switch below).\n\nScope additions:\n\n- Semantics library build: `scripts/export-lean-library.sh` exports only toolchain modules from inside lean4export's checkout, so it cannot export `lean/LeanSharp`. Create `lean/LeanSharp` as a Lake project pinned through `scripts/lib/lean-toolchain.sh`, with lean4export at `$LEAN4EXPORT_COMMIT` as a dependency, plus a script that builds it and runs `lake env lean4export LeanSharp`. Record the bundle hash.\n- Open enums (if Q3 keeps them open): a `switch` expression without a `_` arm throws `SwitchExpressionException` for unnamed values, and M4 has no exception model. Reject such switches with a diagnostic until M6.\n\nCheckpoints, in order:\n\n1. `LeanSharp.Vir` and its canonical encoding, with round-trip and hash-stability tests.\n2. Semantics library v0 bundle built, admitted by the kernel, and passing CLR-agreement tests.\n3. Vertical slice: one method (e.g. `int Abs(int)`) from Roslyn through translation to a kernel-closed parameterless theorem.\n4. Corpus expanded to records, enums and the `Validate` method, plus the expected rejections.\n5. Differential-test generators and the cross-check step for translated output.","files":null}]}